-- title:
--   Uₚ acts through an automorphism on the étale Igusa component
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a valuation subring $Pl$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ together with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$, and an intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ with $K = \mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,L\,(\mathrm{x1FunctionField}(Mp))$, i.e. $K$ is the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Fix further a discrete valuation ring $A$ which is a domain with fraction field $L$, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $A$ acting on $K$ compatibly, and an element $j \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the coefficient embedding of the classical $j$-series [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), with $j \neq 0$. Throughout, $X = \mathrm{TwoChartModel}\,A\,K\,j$ denotes the two-chart model, glued from $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the integral closures $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ and $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}$ of $A[j]$, resp. $A[j^{-1}]$, in $K$, and $\mathrm{modelTo}\,A\,K\,j : X \to \mathrm{Spec}\,A$ is its structure morphism. The residue field of $Pl$ is assumed algebraically closed of characteristic $p$ and an $A$-algebra, and $\mathrm{Pl}$ is assumed to lie over $p$ (the hypothesis `hPl`: $p$ is a non-unit of $Pl$), with a ring map $\rho : A \to Pl$ lifting the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`hρ`) and inducing the $A$-algebra structure on the residue field (`hAlgκ`).
--
--   The remaining data and hypotheses fall into the following groups; each is named and its content summarised.
--
--   (i) *Special fibre as a union of two Igusa components.* Two schemes $C_1, C_2$ proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral over the residue field $\kappa$ of $Pl$, closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ of them into the base change $X_\kappa$ over $\kappa$, the hypothesis `hcover` that every point of $X_\kappa$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, the hypothesis `hred` that the scheme-theoretic intersection $C_1 \times_{X_\kappa} C_2$ is reduced, and $n$ with `hn`: the number of its points equals $n$, and `hn0`: $0 < n$.
--
--   (ii) *Sections and the relative Picard scheme.* A section $\varepsilon$ of $\mathrm{modelTo}\,A\,K\,j$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$, sections $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2$ of $c_1, c_2$, the hypothesis `hε₁` identifying $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ with the base change of $\varepsilon$; a designation $D$ (a scheme $D.P$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ with a zero section) together with `hrep`: $D$ represents the rigidified relative Picard functor cut out by the fibrewise algebraically-equivalent-to-zero condition, and `hsm`, `hsep`: $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is smooth and separated; `hreps` the corresponding representability over $\kappa$ for $D_\kappa$ and `hPk` the comparison isomorphism of Poincaré bundles under base change; designations $D_1, D_2$ for $c_1, c_2$ with representability hypotheses `hrep₁`, `hrep₂`; a morphism $\nu_2$ from $D_\kappa$ to $D_2$ over $\kappa$ with `hν₂` asserting that pulling the Poincaré bundle of $D_2$ back along $\nu_2$ agrees, after rigidification along $\varepsilon_2$, with the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of $D_\kappa$ along the curve change induced by $i_2$; properness of $\mathrm{modelTo}\,A\,K\,j$; and, over $L$, smoothness `hsmL`, geometric integrality `hgiL` of $X_L$, properness `hprL` and geometric connectedness `hgcL` of $D_L \to \mathrm{Spec}\,L$.
--
--   (iii) *Identification of the geometric generic fibre with $X_1(Mp)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.* Compatible algebra structures on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $A$ and $L$; a curve model $M_\eta$ of $\mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with an isomorphism $e_\eta$ onto $X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ compatible with the structure morphisms (`heη`), the nonemptiness of the finite chart preimage, the $q$-expansion pinning `hMηpin` (elements of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ read on $M_\eta$ through the germ at the generic point have Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of their expansion in $K$), and `hgal`: for every $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism $g$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ fixing $L$ pointwise and every pair of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points related by precomposition with $\mathrm{Spec}(g)$, the associated places correspond under the arithmetic Galois action of $g$ on $\mathrm{x1FunctionField}(Mp)$.
--
--   (iv) *Hecke and diamond data on $J_1(Mp)$.* The hypotheses `hin` (`HeckeDiamondInputsAll`) and `hcomm` (`HeckeDiamondCommuteBar`), providing the Hecke input data at all primes and the diamond automorphisms, and their commutation, so that $J_1(Mp) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of $\mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp)$ is a module over $\mathrm{HeckeAlgOne} = \mathbb{Z}[X_{\mathrm{Primes}\sqcup\mathbb{N}}]$; a semiring action of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ on $A$ compatible with $A \to L$ (`hΓA`).
--
--   (v) *The special fibre of the Néron model, abstractly.* A datum $G$ of type `NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`, consisting of abelian groups $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$, a subgroup $G.\mathrm{torus} \le G.J0s$ and a surjection $G.\mathrm{proj} : G.J0s \to G.JI \times G.JE$ with kernel $G.\mathrm{torus}$; bijections $\mathrm{pts}$, $\mathrm{ptsI}$, $\mathrm{ptsE}$ of $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$ with the $\kappa$-points of $D_\kappa$, $D_1$, $D_2$; additivity hypotheses `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE` (pullbacks of the Poincaré bundles along sums are isomorphic to tensor products) and `hPTS` ($\mathrm{pts}$ is additive and unital for the relative group law); `hproj`, expressing $G.\mathrm{proj}$ through composition with the comparison morphism $D_\kappa \to D_1$ coming from $i_1$ and with $\nu_2$.
--
--   (vi) *Points, operators and Galois action on $D$.* A bijection $\mathrm{gpts}$ between $J_1(Mp)$ and the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $D$; endomorphisms $\varphi(t)$ of $D$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ indexed by $t \in \mathrm{HeckeAlgOne}$; semilinear automorphisms $\tau(s)$ of $D$ over the twist of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ by $s \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$; the hypotheses `hφmul` ($\varphi(t)$ is a homomorphism for the relative group law), `hφpts` ($\mathrm{gpts}$ intertwines the Hecke action with composition by $\varphi(t)$), `hτ1`, `hτmul` ($\tau$ is a monoid action in diagrammatic order), `hτφ` ($\tau$ and $\varphi$ commute), `hgadd` ($\mathrm{gpts}$ is additive) and `hτpts` ($\mathrm{gpts}$ intertwines the Galois action with $\tau$).
--
--   (vii) *Abel–Jacobi data.* Representability `hDL` over $L$, a morphism $\mathrm{ajL}$ from $X_L$ to $D_L$ with `hajLε` (it sends the section to the zero section) and `hajL` (its universal property: pullback of the Poincaré bundle along a point $x$ is the line bundle of the divisor of $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of the section), the comparison `hPL`, a morphism $k_L$ over the base changes with `hkL₁`, `hkL₂`, the composite $\mathrm{ajbar}$ with `hajbar`, `hajbar_over`, a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $\bar\varepsilon$ with `hεbar`, `hεbar_aj`, and `hpts_aj`, which says that for $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x$ and $s$ with $s$ the reduction of $\varepsilon$ there is a degree-zero divisor equal to $[x] - [s]$ whose class corresponds under $\mathrm{gpts}$ to $x$ followed by $\mathrm{ajbar}$.
--
--   (viii) *Operators on the special fibre.* A datum $O$ of type `NeronSpecialFibreOpsV3 G` (Hecke operators, diamonds $\langle b \rangle_p$ and $\langle d \rangle_N$, the Atkin–Lehner involution, the inertia action, $\mathrm{verI}$, $\mathrm{frobE}$, with the compatibilities recorded in that structure) and the four-clause hypothesis `hO` matching them with the $\varphi$'s and $\tau$'s on $D$: the Hecke operator at a prime $\ell$ with $\varphi(\mathrm{heckeGenOne}\,\ell)$, $O.\mathrm{diamondP}\,b$ and $O.\mathrm{diamondN}\,d$ with $\varphi(\mathrm{diamondGen}\,d)$ under the stated congruence conditions on $d$ modulo $M$ and modulo $p$, and $O.\mathrm{inertia}\,b$ with $\tau(s)$ whenever $s\zeta = \zeta^{b}$.
--
--   (ix) *Points over inertia-fixed rings (`hF3`).* For every subgroup $I$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ contained in the inertia subgroup at $Pl$, fixing all $p$-th roots of unity, and of finite index in that inertia subgroup, setting $\mathcal{O}_I = Pl \cap \overline{\mathbb{Q}}^I$, there exist a ring map $\rho_I : A \to \mathcal{O}_I$ lifting the structure map and, writing $\mathrm{dom}$ for the set of $y \in J_1(Mp)$ whose $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point factors through an $\mathcal{O}_I$-point of $D$: $I$ fixes $\mathrm{dom}$ pointwise; the factorisation is unique; $\mathrm{dom}$ contains $0$ and is closed under differences; for every $n > 0$ prime to $p$ the reduction map on $n$-torsion $\mathcal{O}_I$-points is injective and every $n$-torsion $\kappa$-point lifts; and $\mathrm{dom}$ is stable under any Frobenius element at $Pl$ normalising $I$.
--
--   (x) *The Néron-type group subscheme (`h𝒜`).* A scheme $\mathcal{A}$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ with a closed immersion $\iota$ into $D.P$ over the base, such that $\mathcal{A} \to \mathrm{Spec}\,A$ is proper and smooth with connected geometric fibres, $\mathcal{A}$ is stable under the unit, multiplication and inverse of the relative group law on $D$, a point of $J_1(Mp)$ lies in $\mathrm{normFreePartAt}(Mp)\,p$ (the range of the norm-free endomorphism at $p$) exactly when the corresponding $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $D$ factors through $\mathcal{A}$, and $\mathcal{A}$ is stable under every $\varphi(t)$.
--
--   (xi) *Vanishing of the diamond sum (`hF10`).* For every $\kappa$-algebra $T'$ and every $T'$-point $v$ of $D_\kappa$ which factors through $\mathcal{A}$ in the stated sense, the composite of $v$ with $\varphi\big(\sum_{b \in (\mathbb{Z}/p)^\times} \mathrm{diamondGen}\, d_b\big)$, where $d_b$ is the natural number representing the pair $(b, 1)$ under the Chinese remainder isomorphism for $p$ and $M$, is the unit of the relative group law.
--
--   (xii) *Igusa models and $q$-expansion reading.* An integral weight one form $w$ of level $M$ over $\kappa$ (a weight one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ with integral $q$-expansion whose reduction is nonzero), the Igusa function field $\mathrm{igusaFunctionFieldX1C}\,\kappa\,M\,w$ obtained by adjoining the inverse of that reduction, curve models $\mathrm{Mdl}_1, \mathrm{Mdl}_2$ of it with isomorphisms $e_1, e_2$ onto $C_1, C_2$ compatible with the structure morphisms (`he₁`, `he₂`), nonemptiness of the relevant chart preimage on $C_1$, the Gauss-reading hypothesis `hgauss₁` (for $a$ in $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ and power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $\bar y \neq 0$ and $a \cdot y = x$ in $L((q))$, the function read off $a$ on $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$ has Laurent expansion $\bar x / \bar y$), the hypothesis `hεC₂` that the reduced section avoids $C_2$, and `hεgal` (compatibility of $\varepsilon$ with any Galois twist of the two-chart model inducing the coefficient map on $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$).
--
--   (xiii) *Raynaud's description of the special fibre Picard group (`hF4c`).* A finite set $\mathrm{nodesIg}$ of pairs of places of the Igusa function field, an isomorphism $\Psi$ of $G.J0s$ with $\mathrm{GluedPic}^0$ of the Igusa function field along $\mathrm{nodesIg}$, isomorphisms $\theta_1, \theta_2$ of $G.JI$, $G.JE$ with $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the Igusa function field, and the seven clauses of `hF4c`: $\mathrm{nodesIg}$ consists exactly of the pairs of places cut out by the $\kappa$-points of $C_1 \times_{X_\kappa} C_2$; its cardinality is $n$; both projections are injective on it; $\mathrm{toPic0Pair} \circ \Psi$ equals $(\theta_1, \theta_2) \circ G.\mathrm{proj}$; the image of $G.\mathrm{torus}$ under $\Psi$ is the range of the node-unit homomorphism; and $\theta_1$, $\theta_2$ are computed by Abel–Jacobi on $C_1$, $C_2$ relative to $\varepsilon_1$, $\varepsilon_2$.
--
--   (xiv) *Frobenius on the Igusa function field.* A semilinear automorphism $\mathrm{frobT}$ of the Igusa function field over $\kappa$ with `hfrobT`: it raises every Laurent coefficient to the $p$-th power.
--
--   (xv) *The abstract specialisation family.* For each admissible inertia subgroup $I$ as in (ix), a subgroup $\mathrm{dom}\mathcal{D}\,I \le J_1(Mp)$ and an additive map $\mathrm{sp}\mathcal{D}\,I$ from it to $\mathrm{GluedPic}^0$ along $\mathrm{nodesIg}$, subject to the two-clause interface `hIFm`: membership in $\mathrm{dom}\mathcal{D}\,I$ is factorisation of the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point through $\mathcal{O}_I$ (for the map chosen by `hF3`), and $\mathrm{sp}\mathcal{D}\,I\,y$ is $\Psi$ of the $\kappa$-point obtained by reducing any such factorisation; and the two-clause hypothesis `hlev`, asserting for $J \le I$ both that an $\mathcal{O}_I$-factorisation induces an $\mathcal{O}_J$-factorisation with the same reduction, and that $\mathrm{dom}\mathcal{D}\,I \subseteq \mathrm{dom}\mathcal{D}\,J$ with $\mathrm{sp}\mathcal{D}\,J = \mathrm{sp}\mathcal{D}\,I$ on it.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion asserts the existence of an additive automorphism $\Phi$ of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of $\mathrm{igusaFunctionFieldX1C}\,\kappa\,M\,w$ with the following property: for all admissible inertia subgroups $I$ and $I'$ (each contained in the inertia subgroup at $Pl$, fixing all $p$-th roots of unity, and of finite index in it), for every $y$ in $\mathrm{normFreePartAt}(Mp)\,p$ with $y \in \mathrm{dom}\mathcal{D}\,I$ and $\mathrm{heckeOperatorOneBar}(Mp)\,p\,y \in \mathrm{dom}\mathcal{D}\,I'$, the second component of $\mathrm{toPic0Pair}$ applied to $\mathrm{sp}\mathcal{D}\,I'$ of $U_p y$ equals $\Phi$ of the second component of $\mathrm{toPic0Pair}$ applied to $\mathrm{sp}\mathcal{D}\,I$ of $y$. In particular the same $\Phi$ works for all pairs $(I, I')$ and all such $y$.
--
--   This is the clause of the semistable-specialisation package for $J_1(Mp)$ at $p$ which records that, on the component of the glued Picard group belonging to the étale Igusa curve, the operator $U_p$ acts on specialised norm-free classes through a single additive automorphism of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the Igusa function field (classically $U_p = \langle p \rangle_* \mathrm{Fr}_*$ there). It is used by [`ModularCurve.exists_qExpSemistableSpecializationPinnedV3_family_normFreePart_and_diamond_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd_of_le_div`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_qExpSemistableSpecializationPinnedV3_family_normFreePart_and_diamond_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd_of_le_div), which assembles the full specialisation datum entering the level-lowering argument at $p$.
